  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical non-conducting solid spheres of same mass and charge are suspended in air from a common point by two non-conducting, massless strings of same length. At equilibrium, the angle between the strings is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>. The spheres are now immersed in a dielectric liquid of density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> and dielectric constant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn></math>. If the angle between the strings remains the same after the immersion, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jUkO0",
      "text": "electric force between the spheres remains unchanged",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FrGqU",
      "text": "electric force between the spheres reduces",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5Op4L",
      "text": "mass density of the spheres is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>840</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Vg2MF",
      "text": "the tension in the strings holding the spheres remains unchanged",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/c3f344e5-59ef-4ffb-80dd-72d6763317e5-image.png\"/></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>;</mo><mo> </mo><mi>T</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p><p>Divide,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>As force between two charged bodies doesn't depend upon medium. Hence, the force between them remains same because the distance spheres is same.</p><p>When it is submerged in liquid then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">'</mo></msup><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Divide,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">mg</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Equating (1) & (2)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>  </mo><mo>;</mo><mo>  </mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>800</mn><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>21</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>840</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>21</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
